"blackears","id":6724608,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjQ2MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6724608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears","html_url":"https://github.com/blackears","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T19:56:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T19:56:25Z","body":"I just tried Godot 4.4 rc 1 and it's happening there too.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676371500/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781019009","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103158#issuecomment-2781019009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103158","id":2781019009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lwvuB","user":{"login":"repunchpunch","id":74110988,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MTEwOTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74110988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch","html_url":"https://github.com/repunchpunch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/repunchpunch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T17:59:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T17:59:01Z","body":"ver. 4.4.1\nArea3D.has_overlapping_bodies() doesn't detect StaticBody3D. Even though StaticBody3D inherits PhysicsBody3D and Area3D.has_overlapping_bodies() must detect any PhysicsBody3D, as stated in it's Doc paragraph (no issues with Rigidbody3D). The workaround is to add Area3D to a StaticBody3D and use Area3D.has_overlapping_areas(), which works just fine.\n_IMHO_ at least mention of that \"feature\" must be added, if fix is too complicated.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781019009/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2805559099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103158#issuecomment-2805559099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103158","id":2805559099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nOW87","user":{"login":"blackears","id":6724608,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjQ2MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6724608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears","html_url":"https://github.com/blackears","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blackears/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T14:39:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T14:39:48Z","body":"After some more research, it seems that for Jolt, you need to specifically enable this in the project properties.  You need to click on Advance Settings, then Physics > Jolt Physics 3D > Areas Detect Static Bodies.  This is disabled by default to prevent Area3Ds from consuming CPU cycles.  I think the idea is to make these checks with ray casts where possible.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2805559099/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]